# Prettier governs the code this migration owns: src/lib, src/routes, and the root config files.
# Everything below is either generated, or hand-maintained prose and CSS that predates it — and
# reformatting those wholesale would bury real changes in diffs nobody can review.

# Build output and dependencies
node_modules
dist
.svelte-kit
build

# Generated backend JavaScript (compiled from the .ts sources)
backend/**/*.js
backend/**/*.js.map

# The Express backend keeps the formatting it was written with. It was not part of the Svelte
# migration, and reformatting fifteen files wholesale would bury the handful of real changes made
# to it. Same reasoning as its ESLint exemption in eslint.config.js.
backend/**/*.ts
tsconfig.backend.json
nodemon.json

# The design system. styles.css and responsive.css are hand-maintained, heavily sectioned, and
# responsive.css in particular documents *why* each rule exists — Prettier would reflow all of it
# and the comments would stop lining up with the rules they explain.
src/css

# Runtime data and lockfiles
data
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Prose, notes and plans — written for people, wrapped by hand
*.md
docs
tasks
dev
.claude

# The captured copy of the host's live compose file. It is committed byte-identical so that
#     diff <(ssh rmi-services cat /srv/winner-app/compose.yml) deploy/compose.rmi-services.yml
# means something; reformatting it would silently destroy the one property it exists to have.
deploy/compose.rmi-services.yml

# Standalone helpers and config that predate this setup
test-console.cjs
test-texting.html
public/manifest.json
docker-compose.yml
